+# Building RenderDoc with Python 3.12
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```powershell
+# One command - installs Python 3.12 via uv, builds Release x64
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File build_py312.ps1
+```
+
+Or for the full release pipeline (x64 + Win32 + pack):
+
+```cmd
+release.bat
+```
+
+---
+
+## How It Works
+
+### Python 3.12 via uv
+
+The build uses `uv` to manage a clean Python 3.12 installation. The first run of `build_py312.ps1` will:
+
+1. Call `uv python install 3.12.13` to get a pristine CPython
+2. Prepare a build directory at `<repo_root>/py312-build/` with the files `python.props` expects:
+   - `include/Python.h` (headers)
+   - `python312.lib` (import library)
+   - `python312.zip` (standard library, zipped from `Lib/`)
+   - `python312.dll`
+
+### python.props Detection
+
+`qrenderdoc/Code/pyrenderdoc/python.props` checks for a custom Python via:
+
+1. `VSPythonOverridePath` MSBuild property (used in our scripts)
+2. `RENDERDOC_PYTHON_PREFIX64` / `RENDERDOC_PYTHON_PREFIX32` environment variables
+3. Default bundled Python 3.6 in `qrenderdoc/3rdparty/python/`
+
+It auto-detects the version by checking for `python312.lib`, `python312.zip`, and `include/Python.h`.
+
+---
+
+## Scripts
+
+| Script | Purpose |
+|--------|---------|
+| `build_py312.ps1` | Full build: installs Python 3.12 via uv, builds Release x64 solution |
+| `build_py312.bat` | Build Release x64 only (assumes `py312-build/` already exists) |
+| `release.bat` | Full release pipeline: x64 + Win32 + Python modules + fast_injector + pack |
+| `pack.bat` | Pack build output into `dist/` and create `.7z` archive |
+| `pack_dist.py` | Python script that copies files and creates the archive |
+
+---
+
+## Manual Setup (without scripts)
+
+If you want to set up Python 3.12 manually:
+
+```powershell
+# Install via uv
+uv python install 3.12.13
+
+# Find the path
+$pyRoot = Split-Path (uv python find 3.12.13)
+
+# Prepare build directory
+$buildDir = "D:\git\renderdoc\py312-build"
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $buildDir -Force
+Copy-Item -Recurse "$pyRoot\include" "$buildDir\include"
+Copy-Item "$pyRoot\libs\python312.lib" "$buildDir\python312.lib"
+Copy-Item "$pyRoot\python312.dll" "$buildDir\python312.dll"
+Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem
+[System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory("$pyRoot\Lib", "$buildDir\python312.zip")
+```
+
+Then build:
+
+```powershell
+msbuild renderdoc.sln /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=x64 /p:VSPythonOverridePath="D:\git\renderdoc\py312-build" /m /v:minimal
+```
+
+---
+
+## Verify
+
+After a successful build, you should see:
+
+```
+Built against python from D:\git\renderdoc\py312-build
+```
+
+Output files:
+
+```
+x64\Release\pymodules\
+├── renderdoc.pyd       (Core API)
+├── renderdoc.lib
+├── renderdoc.pdb
+├── qrenderdoc.pyd      (Qt UI API)
+├── qrenderdoc.lib
+└── qrenderdoc.pdb
+```
+
+Test import:
+
+```python
+import sys, os
+sys.path.insert(0, r'x64\Release\pymodules')
+os.add_dll_directory(r'x64\Release')
+import renderdoc as rd
+print(rd.CullMode.FrontAndBack)  # 3
+```
+
+---
+
+## Platform Toolset
+
+- **v145** = project default (VS 2015 compatible)
+- Current VS 18 MSBuild handles this automatically; no override needed.
+
+---
+
+## renderdoc-mcp Integration
+
+The built `renderdoc.pyd` and `qrenderdoc.pyd` are compatible with Python 3.12. To use with renderdoc-mcp:
+
+1. Add `x64\Release\pymodules\` to `PYTHONPATH`
+2. Or copy `.pyd` files into your Python 3.12 environment's `site-packages`
+3. Ensure `rhdoc.dll` is accessible via `os.add_dll_directory()` or PATH
+
+---
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+| Issue | Solution |
+|-------|----------|
+| `ImportError: DLL load failed` | Python version mismatch - rebuild with matching Python |
+| `uv not found` | Install uv: `irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 \| iex` |
+| `MSBuild not found` | Check VS install path in scripts |
+| `python312.zip missing` | `build_py312.ps1` creates it automatically |
+| `Python.h not found` | Verify `py312-build/include/Python.h` exists |
+
+---
+
+## References
+
+- `qrenderdoc/Code/pyrenderdoc/python.props` - Python version detection logic
+- `qrenderdoc/Code/pyrenderdoc/pyrenderdoc_module.vcxproj` - pyrenderdoc project
+- `qrenderdoc/Code/pyrenderdoc/qrenderdoc_module.vcxproj` - qrenderdoc module project
